{
  "_comment": [
    "The event emission policy (PGSS §6.9): Machine\\Generic\\Events holds",
    "one key per event-type segment, any of which may carry an Enabled",
    "REG_DWORD of 0 or 1; the deepest on a type's path decides, and the",
    "type's tier decides where none does -- standard on, verbose and debug",
    "off. Essential types never consult it.",
    "",
    "This seed sets no Enabled anywhere: with nothing set, the tiers decide,",
    "which is the policy a machine ships with. It creates the key so the",
    "policy has a home an administrator writes beneath, and so the key's",
    "descriptor has something to ride on:",
    "",
    "    S:(AL;CI;0x10002;;;WD)",
    "",
    "a SYSTEM_ALARM ACE for Everyone, inherited by every key beneath, over",
    "KEY_SET_VALUE (0x2) | DELETE (0x10000). A handle opened for writing",
    "anywhere in the tree carries that continuous-audit mask, so each change",
    "to what is recorded is itself recorded (PGSS §6.9: a SACL that audits",
    "writes). Only the SACL is given; the owner and DACL stay inherited from",
    "the Machine hive (Administrators and SYSTEM full, Authenticated Users",
    "read), which is what §6.9 asks for. Setting a SACL needs",
    "SeSecurityPrivilege, which autoapply, running as SYSTEM, holds.",
    "",
    "Every emitter reads the tree: the kernel (kmes/event_policy.c, a watch",
    "on this key, a change applied within about 50 ms plus one walk), and",
    "libpeios, peios-rs and libp-go for userspace components.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the kernel package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply. Until it is applied the key does",
    "not exist, every emitter still decides by tier, and the kernel keeps its",
    "machine-root fallback watch armed to notice the key being created."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Events",
      "descriptor": "S:(AL;CI;0x10002;;;WD)"
    }
  ]
}
